; closure-callee-band.fk — a call whose callee is a closure the call site just built keeps it while its arguments walk.
;
; A call of a capturing nested defn by name builds its closure at the call site (tag 243 under tag 244) and
; holds that fn-value in a C local while the arguments are walked. A melt hands back a closure row no root names,
; and the next closure to be made takes the row under the same word, so an argument whose walk melts and then makes
; closures of its own would leave the callee another closure's captures. The indirect call now leaves its callee
; on the value stack until the call runs.
;
; The argument here burns four heaps of pairs (at least four million; the heap's capacity is kernel_live word 13, and a
; process that ran other work first has grown it, so a fixed four million melted twice in a band sweep's shard) -- several
; melts, counted in kernel_live word 21 -- and then calls a capturing nested defn eighty times, which takes eighty rows
; from the ones the melts handed back (the last in first out, so the callee's is among them). The callee must still add
; what IT captured.
;
; Verdict 7
; REQUIRES: fkwu's melt count (kernel_live word 21)
; plant: -DFK_PLANT_NOCALLEE reads 2 (the callee answers 125 where it captured 3: the row another closure took)
;
;   1   the callee adds what it captured (k = 3) after the argument's melts and its own eighty closures
;   2   the argument's walk melted at least three times
;   4   a second call, k = 40, answers its own capture too: the rows are not shared by the two
(do
    (defn ccb-junk (n) (if (le n 0) (list) (cons n (ccb-junk (sub n 1)))))
    (defn ccb-drain (n sum) (if (le n 0) sum (ccb-drain (sub n 1) (add sum (len (ccb-junk 1000))))))
    (defn ccb-gen () (nth (kernel_live (host_pid)) 21))
    ; a call of a capturing nested defn: the call site builds a closure row, and the row goes back when the call is done
    (defn ccb-take (j) (do (defn g (x) (add x j)) (g 1)))
    (defn ccb-take-many (n) (if (le n 0) 0 (do (ccb-take (add n 100)) (ccb-take-many (sub n 1)))))
    (defn ccb-rounds () (do (let four (div (mul (nth (kernel_live (host_pid)) 13) 4) 1000)) (if (gt four 4000) four 4000)))
    (defn ccb-heavy () (do (let burn (ccb-drain (ccb-rounds) 0)) (let others (ccb-take-many 80)) 5))
    (defn ccb-run (k) (do (defn inner (x) (add x k)) (inner (ccb-heavy))))
    (defn ccb-bit (ok bit) (if ok bit 0))

    (let g0 (ccb-gen))
    (let first (ccb-run 3))
    (let g1 (ccb-gen))
    (let second (ccb-run 40))
    (print (list "closure-callee" first second "melts" (sub g1 g0)))
    (add (ccb-bit (eq first 8) 1)
    (add (ccb-bit (ge (sub g1 g0) 3) 2)
         (ccb-bit (eq second 45) 4)))
)
